@devin-ai-integration Thanks for the pass. Flagging that the PR has changed materially since you reviewed it, in case that is worth a re-run.

Vex caught a real accessibility hole in what you reviewed: `shortcut` was rendered `aria-hidden` while `aria-keyshortcuts` stayed an independently optional prop, so a row could draw a visible binding that assistive tech never heard about, and one of the stories did exactly that.

Fixed in 3b708544d0. `shortcut` now takes an Electron accelerator rather than pre-rendered glyphs, and the row derives both the drawn hint and `aria-keyshortcuts` from that single value, so the two cannot disagree. `ActionMenu.Item` dropped its `ariaKeyShortcuts` prop as a result. New coverage in `menu-item-aside.test.tsx` plus an assertion on the composed row in the `ItemSlots` story.

@codex review e600dd0ece

Your P1 on the nested middleware was correct and this is the fix. `onboardingCompletedMiddleware` resolved on `url.pathname` alone while `authMiddleware` uses `url.pathname + url.search`; since the nested pass owns `/assistant/onboarding/*`, the marker was stripped before the guard read it and the exemption was dead on the real route. Now passes path and query, matching `authMiddleware`.

Regression coverage is at the middleware level and seeds the resolved-assistants store so `alreadyOnboarded` is genuinely true. The resolver-level tests structurally could not catch this: they hand the query straight to `resolveNavigation`.

@vex-assistant-bot Addressed in f83869a3cb.

**Blocking finding (English-only confirmation copy):** converted the whole control's copy in one piece. `POLICY_COPY` in `channel-trust-floor-section.tsx` maps every admission policy to catalog keys for its dropdown label, description, and (where gated) confirmation title/message/action; all keys added to en/es/ru. All three gated policies resolve their dialogs through the shared control via those keys, type-checked against the catalog by the `i18next` augmentation. I went wider than the confirmations alone because leaving `POLICY_LABELS`/`getPolicyDescriptions` hardcoded would have had translated dialogs quoting untranslated dropdown labels; both are deleted from `lib/channel-admission-policy/types.ts`, whose remit is the cross-surface contract, not web copy. `confirmFallback` now only guards the close-animation frame.

Also merged `origin/main` (07edb5edc4): the widened `src/**` i18n ratchet from #41368 lands cleanly with this, and there is no overlap with the regions #41366 touches.
